From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:51:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(server): pass skip_gzip responses through from response
 start

Starlette 1.8.0 checks the gzip responder's exclusion flag on
http.response.start, but our skip_gzip opt-out only set it on the first
body message. Binary file reads (images, PDFs) and downloads then never
sent their start message, and the server answered 500, so the FileViewer
showed "Error loading file: 500" for every image. The server image
installs without the lockfile, so it picks up Starlette 1.8.0.

Squashed copy of upstream PR #10585 (issue #10481), which also hardens
the download proxy's stream cleanup and runner-offline errors.

Not upstream yet: pulled from upstream PR #10585; drop this copy once it merges.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Docs: none (fix: images and PDFs load in the file viewer again; no setting)
---
